## 3. RECOMMENDED TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE

To ensure high performance, sub-second bidding speed, and zero exposure to expensive recurring third-party map bills, the platform is built on an enterprise, cost-controlled stack:

* **Frontend Apps (Passenger & Driver):** Developed in **Next.js (React)** styled with Tailwind CSS, packaged as installable **Progressive Web Apps (PWAs)** with optional lightweight Android APK wrappers. PWAs guarantee immediate access via web link without requiring users to download heavy 80MB files from app stores, consume minimal phone storage, and update instantly without app store review delays.
* **Backend API & Real-Time Sockets:** Built with **Node.js (NestJS)** incorporating high-concurrency **WebSockets**. This handles sub-second fare bidding updates, ride dispatch alerts, and live vehicle location pings with minimal server load.
* **Database & Caching:** **PostgreSQL** provides relational data storage for immutable trip ledgers, receipts, and user records. **Redis** provides lightning-fast in-memory caching for active driver coordinates, live bidding rooms, and session states.
* **Cost-Controlled Geospatial Mapping:** Open-source tile routing (**Leaflet / OpenStreetMap / MapLibre**) ensures map views, distance calculations, and tracking do not generate heavy recurring Google Maps API bills.

